==================================================
1. PROJECT PURPOSE
==================================================

SAATHI is a digital platform designed around SIH Problem Statement 26043.

The core idea is:

Citizens and organizations submit real-world societal problems.
The platform uses AI to understand and structure those problems.
It then semantically matches problems with relevant university faculty/expertise and eventually industry partners.
The platform is intended to support the complete journey from:

Societal Problem
→ AI Analysis
→ Expert/University Matching
→ Industry Collaboration
→ Project Development
→ Impact Tracking

The system is intended for the Jharkhand ecosystem and should connect:

Citizen
Government
University / HEI
Faculty / Experts
Industry / Startup / MSME


==================================================
2. PROBLEM STATEMENT SUMMARY
==================================================

Communities in Jharkhand face many unresolved local challenges involving:

- Education
- Healthcare
- Agriculture
- Water management
- Sanitation
- Environment
- Rural livelihoods
- Accessibility
- Urban infrastructure
- Public service delivery

There is currently no centralized mechanism for citizens to submit these challenges and have them systematically:

- collected
- categorized
- validated
- prioritized
- matched with university expertise
- connected with industry
- tracked through implementation
- evaluated for social impact

Universities have students, faculty, research expertise and innovation capabilities.

Industry has technical expertise, funding, mentorship, prototyping and deployment capabilities.

SAATHI aims to connect these fragmented stakeholders through one platform.


