30. DEVELOPMENT STYLE
==================================================

The project is being built incrementally.

Do not dump the entire final system at once.

Prefer:

Build one component
→ test it
→ integrate it
→ move to next component.

The user confirms when something works.
When the user says something works, accept that as confirmation and move forward rather than repeatedly asking for screenshots or validation.

The user is comfortable with VS Code, Postman, PostgreSQL/pgAdmin and Docker but may need clear step-by-step instructions for unfamiliar backend/ML concepts.

When modifying existing code, clearly identify which file is being changed and provide the exact relevant code.

Avoid unnecessary complexity and unnecessary dependencies.